area: config
case: 63-bool-string-upper
verification: explicit-divergence
oracle: python
projection: config
reason: the port refuses a boolean spelled as a string or as a number. TOML has one boolean type with two words; pydantic reads twelve spellings, and D-E in plans/duplication-and-simplification-plan.md records why the port does not: a value of the wrong type is a typo and the loader reports it rather than re-typing it. The extractor-default difference every other config golden records is folded into the refusal.
--- oracle
default=serper
permitted=-
providers_defaulted=false
enabled=serper
effective=serper
free_only=false
missing_keys=serper
missing_agent=
policy,500,2000,10.000000
fetch,true,trafilatura,15.000000,8388608,40000,200,6000,3,false,false,seekwright/0.1.1 (+https://github.com/leoschwarz/seekwright),-,false,http,-,-,-,60.000000,-,268435456,33554432,300.000000
search,-,-,60.000000,3,120.000000
agent,false,-,-,90.000000,30.000000,24000,500,2500,0.250000,-,-
logging,INFO,text,WARNING,false,false,false
dashboard,true,-
provider serper enabled=true cost=- depth=standard output=sourcedAnswer mode=fast url=- cooldown=60.000000 app=- index=- title_attr=- url_attr=- snippet_attr=-
--- port
ERR providers.serper.enabled: expected a boolean, found 'TRUE'
